{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-123741" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $R=[1,3]\\times [-2,-1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=10+y-3x.$ Further, let \n\n$$\nI={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nbe the unique number such that over all rectangular partitions $P$ of $R,$ we have \n$L(f,P)\\,\\le I\\,\\le U(f,P),$\nwhere $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P)$ are the corresponding lower and upper Riemann sums, and \n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\,.\n$$\n\nWhat expression is missing from the double summation above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080762/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bf7ab7bbd22eedd50c81f62a6b45e9dc0d84734872ecbff57379d00727a31a7"} {"question" "q-123741" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe need to compute $U(f,P).$ \n\nNotice that for all subregions ${R}_{ij},$ we have that\n\n- $f(x,y)=10+y-3x$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=10+y-3x$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top left corner* of each subregion. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{M}_{ij}=f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j})=10+{y}_{j}-3{x}_{i-1}\n$$\n\nand the upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(10+{y}_{j}-3{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $10+{y}_{j}-3{x}_{i-1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080762/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bf7ab7bbd22eedd50c81f62a6b45e9dc0d84734872ecbff57379d00727a31a7"} {"question" "q-123741" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080762/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "90696914361c3f2bd2d92ca1c6f87812f505e284a8674f333d2493737ab1e3fc"} {"question" "q-123741" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080762/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bf7ab7bbd22eedd50c81f62a6b45e9dc0d84734872ecbff57379d00727a31a7"} {"question" "q-123741" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10+{y}_{j-1}-3{x}_{i-1}"] ["math" "10+{y}_{j-1}-3{x}_{i}"] ["math" "10+{y}_{j}-3{x}_{i-1}"] ["math" "10+{y}_{j}-3{x}_{i}"] ["text" "None of the options is correct"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080762/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bf7ab7bbd22eedd50c81f62a6b45e9dc0d84734872ecbff57379d00727a31a7"} {"question" "q-123741" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10+{y}_{j}-3{x}_{i-1}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080762/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bf7ab7bbd22eedd50c81f62a6b45e9dc0d84734872ecbff57379d00727a31a7"} {"question" "q-123742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $R=[1,2]\\times [2,6]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+y.$ Further, let \n\n$$\nI={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nbe the unique number such that over all rectangular partitions $P$ of $R,$ we have \n$L(f,P)\\,\\le I\\,\\le U(f,P),$\nwhere $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P)$ are the corresponding lower and upper Riemann sums, and \n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\,.\n$$\n\nWhat expression is missing from the double summation above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080762/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bf7ab7bbd22eedd50c81f62a6b45e9dc0d84734872ecbff57379d00727a31a7"} {"question" "q-123742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe need to compute $L(f,P).$ \n\nNotice that for all subregions ${R}_{ij},$ we have that\n\n- $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+y$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{m}_{ij}=f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})={x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}\n$$\n\nand the lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is ${x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080762/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bf7ab7bbd22eedd50c81f62a6b45e9dc0d84734872ecbff57379d00727a31a7"} {"question" "q-123742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080762/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "90696914361c3f2bd2d92ca1c6f87812f505e284a8674f333d2493737ab1e3fc"} {"question" "q-123742" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080762/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bf7ab7bbd22eedd50c81f62a6b45e9dc0d84734872ecbff57379d00727a31a7"} {"question" "q-123742" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}"] ["math" "{x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j}^{2}+{y}_{j}"] ["math" "{x}_{i}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}"] ["math" "{x}_{i}^{2}+2{y}_{j}^{2}+{y}_{j}"] ["text" "None of the options is correct"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080762/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bf7ab7bbd22eedd50c81f62a6b45e9dc0d84734872ecbff57379d00727a31a7"} {"question" "q-123742" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080762/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bf7ab7bbd22eedd50c81f62a6b45e9dc0d