 "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080762/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bf7ab7bbd22eedd50c81f62a6b45e9dc0d84734872ecbff57379d00727a31a7"} {"question" "q-123846" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nNow, since ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=6,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)=U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}6\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =6({\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}) \\\\  & =6(7-1)(6-4) \\\\  & =6\\cdot 6\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =72.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=72\\le {∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\le 72=U(f,P)\n$$\n\nwhich implies that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=72.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080762/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bf7ab7bbd22eedd50c81f62a6b45e9dc0d84734872ecbff57379d00727a31a7"} {"question" "q-123846" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080762/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "90696914361c3f2bd2d92ca1c6f87812f505e284a8674f333d2493737ab1e3fc"} {"question" "q-123846" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/ra